    "ULS_the_strangest_machine": "The Strangest Machine",
    "ULS_the_strangest_machine_desc": "Neil Blaney, the minister for the Northern Counties, has replicated his enormous success at Donegal establishing a Fianna Fáil political machine, this time in Ulster. How, precisely, he has done so remains a mystery to the Dublin government he nominally responds to. While his methods are admittedly shady, no one can complain he doesn't maintain “law and order”...",
    "ULS_rifles_round_every_corner": "Rifles 'Round Every Corner",
    "ULS_rifles_round_every_corner_desc": "The tortuous and slow conquest of British Ulster enabled the planned creation of the stay-behind Auxiliary Units to succeed, unlike what was the case elsewhere in Britain. Dozens, if not hundreds of armament depots are spread out throughout the territory of the Northern Counties, providing ample supplies of weaponry to the Auxiliaries, which over time have evolved into protestant resistance groups, known under the umbrella name of the “Ulster Volunteer Force”.",
